# Symbols errcheck may ignore, with the reason each cannot fail. Passed with
# -excludeonly, so THIS FILE IS THE COMPLETE EXCLUSION SET: errcheck's own
# ~19 bundled DefaultExcludedSymbols do not apply. That is the point - a
# bundled list nobody can see is the false comfort this invariant exists to
# remove, and it silenced the fmt.Print family where a broken pipe is a real
# failure.
#
# Only provably infallible symbols belong here. If a symbol can fail on any
# reachable path, handle it instead of listing it.

# (*bytes.Buffer).Write never fails: it grows the buffer or panics on
# allocation failure, which is fatal either way.
(*bytes.Buffer).Write
(*bytes.Buffer).WriteByte
(*bytes.Buffer).WriteString

# (*strings.Builder) is documented never to return an error from its Write
# methods, for the same reason: it grows or it panics.
(*strings.Builder).Write
(*strings.Builder).WriteByte
(*strings.Builder).WriteRune
(*strings.Builder).WriteString
